-- title:
--   (varpi) prime and 𝔪=(varpi,j-x) at a smooth point
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ with decidable equality, and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red}\colon A\to k$. Let $a\in k$ satisfy $a^{q^2}\neq a$, let $K$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ that is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb Q$, and write $A_0=\mathtt{coeffSubring}\,A\,K=A\cap K$, with $\mathrm{red}_0=\mathtt{redRestrict}$ the restriction of $\mathrm{red}$ to $A_0$. Assume given $x\in A_0$ with $\mathrm{red}_0(x)=a$ and $\varpi\in A_0$ such that for every $c\in A_0$ one has $\mathrm{red}_0(c)=0$ exactly when $c=\varpi d$ for some $d\in A_0$. Let $R_0=\mathtt{modularLocalizedAtPoint}$ be the subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-Laurent series consisting of those $f$ for which there are $r,s\in A_0[X_0,X_1]$ with $f\cdot\mathtt{modularEval}(s)=\mathtt{modularEval}(r)$ and $\mathtt{pointEval}(s)\neq 0$; here $\mathtt{modularEval}$ substitutes the $q$-expansions $X_0\mapsto j$, $X_1\mapsto j(\mathfrak q^{q})$ with coefficients included as constant series, and $\mathtt{pointEval}$ evaluates via $\mathrm{red}_0$ at $(a,a^{q})$. The conclusion is twofold: the ideal of $R_0$ generated by the image of $\varpi$ is prime; and, for any local-ring structure on $R_0$, its maximal ideal is generated by the images of $\varpi$ and of $X_0-x$, i.e. by $\varpi$ and $j-x$.
--
--   This describes the local ring of the plane model of $X_0(q)$ at a point $(a,a^{q})$ of its special fibre lying on the branch $j_q=j^{q}$ but not on the branch $j=j_q^{q}$: the special fibre of the local ring is a domain and the maximal ideal needs only the two generators $\varpi$ and $j-x$, so the ring is a two-dimensional regular local ring. It feeds the integral-closedness statement for these local rings and the accompanying membership criterion for integral elements.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_isPrime_span_uniformizer_and_maximalIdeal_modularLocalizedAtPoint_eq_of_pow_sq_ne.lean

